## 6. ShareAlike Requirement

If a Modified Work or derivative work based on the Work is publicly released, it must be made available under licensing conditions that are **substantially equivalent to those of this License**.

In particular, a distributor may not:

- change the Modified Work to a license that permits unauthorized Commercial Use;
- remove the Non-Commercial restriction;
- remove the attribution requirement;
- remove the modification-notice requirement;
- otherwise circumvent the core conditions of this License.

A modifier may provide additional copyright notices or compatibility statements for their own original contributions, provided that such terms do not conflict with the requirements above.

---

## 7. Source Code of Modified Works

This License does **not** require a modifier to automatically publish or disclose their modified source code merely because they have modified the Work.

However, if the modifier publicly releases the modified source code, that source code must remain subject to this License.

If a modifier releases only binary files, compiled outputs, or other non-source forms, this License does not automatically require disclosure of the corresponding source code.

Any publicly released version must nevertheless comply with the Non-Commercial and ShareAlike requirements of this License.

